    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Evaluate\n$$\\frac1{\\sqrt2+\\sqrt1}+\\frac1{\\sqrt3+\\sqrt2}+\\cdots+\\frac1{\\sqrt{100}+\\sqrt{99}}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$9$\n\nRationalise each term; the intermediate roots cancel.",
      "worked": "For each term,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1{\\sqrt{n+1}+\\sqrt n}&=\\frac{\\sqrt{n+1}-\\sqrt n}{(n+1)-n}\\\\\\frac1{\\sqrt{n+1}+\\sqrt n}&=\\sqrt{n+1}-\\sqrt n.\\end{align*}$$\nWriting the required sum as $S$,\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=(\\sqrt2-\\sqrt1)+(\\sqrt3-\\sqrt2)+\\cdots+(\\sqrt{100}-\\sqrt{99})\\\\S&=\\sqrt{100}-\\sqrt1\\\\S&=9.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 62
  },
